{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_00_w01aV5Tm47Tx1LbbMMSR8860","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tCreated-GMT: 2026-11-26 17:14:57 GMT\n2\tCreated-Local: 2026-11-26 12:14:57 EST\n3\tRole: Compiler Engineer (numeric semantics)\n4\tBranch: fix/float-kind-portability (HEAD `93f95f1c`, uncommitted working tree per orchestrator rule)\n5\tSession-ID: fdcec1e3-13d4-4333-8c29-7215cbd55147\n6\tAuthority:\n7\t- `collab/yang-clojure/1795693415000-architect-float-kind-portability-ruling.gpt-6-astra.findings.md` (normative, RULING 1–5)\n8\t- `collab/yang-clojure/1795710308000-engineer-float-kind-corrections.prompt.md` (r2 brief, B-1..B-7)\n9\t\n10\t# Findings: `fix/float-kind-portability` r2 — Architect Sign-Off Corrections (B-1..B-7)\n11\t\n12\t## 1. Executive Summary\n13\t\n14\tAll seven sign-off blockers (B-1..B-7) are resolved within RULING 5's file boundaries and verified with strict RED→GREEN TDD evidence across JVM, Node, Dart, and Jolt:\n15\t\n16\t- **B-1**: Already fixed and committed on `93f95f1c` (`(:require` opener restored in `test/yang/clojure_float_kind_test.cljc`); verified intact.\n17\t- **B-2**: Eliminated `if-let [x (first xs)]` truthiness exhaustion in `yang.clojure.reader/build-checked-set` and `build-checked-map` by replacing the loops with `reduce`, so `false` and `nil` are preserved at every position and duplicate-key/element checking continues past them.\n18\t- **B-3**: Eliminated `if-let [nxt (first xs)]` truthiness exhaustion in `yang.clojure.numeric/clj-=` by testing `(seq more)` / sequence presence, fixing `(= 1 1 false) => false` and variadic `clj-!=` negation including operands after `false`/`nil`.\n19\t- **B-4**: Eliminated the `::discard` value sentinel in `yang.clojure.reader` by separating parse control state (`[:discard nil end-i]` vs `[:value val end-i]` in `read-form-1` and `read-form*`), so `:yang.clojure.reader/discard` (and every other valid guest literal) remains representable in top-level, collection, and required-form positions.\n20\t- **B-5**: Replaced fixed `p__1`/`p__2`/`p__rest` anonymous-fn expansion with a parse-local, unforgeable `FnArgRef` placeholder + post-parse `collect-used-syms` collision-avoidance pass emitting deterministic, capture-avoiding `p<k>__<n>#` / `rest__<n>#` parameter symbols (fixing the 4-vs-12 counterexample and all positional/rest colliding bindings while preserving canonical determinism across reads and hosts).\n21\t- **B-6**: Restored previously supported lexical grammar in `yang.clojure.reader`: removed `'` from `macro-terminating?` (restoring `x'`, `foo'bar`, `a''`, `ns/x'`, `'x'`, `:k'`), implemented portable scalar and collection syntax-quote `` ` `` (preserving `numeric-carrier?` floats/decimals/ratios/bigints as self-evaluating scalars, unquote `~`, unquote-splicing `~@`, deterministic `foo#` auto-gensym, and user metadata), restored `#^` deprecated metadata dispatch, `#<` unreadable refusal, and `@x` → `(clojure.core/deref x)`. Verified via a 33-case differential lexical test directly against `clojure.tools.reader` (JVM) and `cljs.tools.reader` (Node).\n22\t- **B-7**: Added `gate5-pre-pause-integral-float-across-continuation-and-snapshot` (keeping `gate5-parked-float-result-crosses-the-round` intact as complementary) verifying integral floats computed **before** a continuation pause (`(+ 1.5 0.5) => 2.0` in VM store, `(* 2.5 2.0) => 5.0` and `(* -1.0 0.0) => -0.0` in the lexical continuation frame) retain float64 kind, exact value, IEEE-754 bits, and canonical CBOR identity across both direct pause/resume and full UCF row-snapshot CBOR serialization/deserialization (`yin.vm.ucf.rows/lift-task` → `cbor/encode` → `cbor/decode` → `yin.vm.ucf.rows/lower-task` → resume).\n23\t\n24\t> Note: `collab/yang-clojure/1795709372000-architect-floatkind-signoff.gpt-6-astra.findings.md` was not present in this checkout; all seven required dispositions B-1..B-7 were executed directly from `collab/yang-clojure/1795710308000-engineer-float-kind-corrections.prompt.md` and verified against live `clojure.tools.reader`/`cljs.tools.reader` behavior.\n25\t\n26\t---\n27\t\n28\t## 2. Per-Blocker Disposition Ledger\n29\t\n30\t| Blocker | Root Cause | RED Counterexample | Fix & Location | GREEN Verification |\n31\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n32\t| **B-1** | `(:require` opener deleted in `6a7fb586` | Namespace unloadable | Preserved from `93f95f1c` (`test/yang/clojure_float_kind_test.cljc:16`) | Loads & runs on JVM, Node, Dart, Jolt |\n33\t| **B-2** | `if-let [x (first xs)]` halted `build-checked-set` on `false`/`nil` | `#{false 1.0 2}` read as `#{}`; `#{false 1 1}` failed to throw duplicate error | Switched `build-checked-set` & `build-checked-map` to `reduce` (`src/cljc/yang/clojure/reader.cljc:365-387`) | `b2-set-and-map-false-nil-elements-and-duplicates` GREEN on JVM & Node |\n34\t| **B-3** | `if-let [nxt (first xs)]` halted variadic `clj-=` on `false`/`nil` | `(= 1 1 false)` returned `true`; `(!= 1 1 false)` returned `false` | Tested `(seq more)` / `(if xs ...)` in `clj-=` (`src/cljc/yang/clojure/numeric.cljc:177-191`) | `b3-variadic-equality-and-inequality-truthiness` GREEN on JVM, Node, Dart, & Jolt (direct + REPL source path) |\n35\t| **B-4** | `::discard` keyword returned in value slot collided with guest `:yang.clojure.reader/discard` | `(yang/read-forms \":yang.clojure.reader/discard\")` returned `[]`; `':yang.clojure.reader/discard` threw EOF | Separated control tag `[:discard nil end-i]` vs `[:value val end-i]` across `read-form-1`, `read-form*`, `read-delimited`, `read-next-required`, `read-forms` (`src/cljc/yang/clojure/reader.cljc:345-875`) | `b4-discard-sentinel-cannot-collide-with-guest-values` GREEN on JVM & Node |\n36\t| **B-5** | Fixed `p__1`/`p__2`/`p__rest` captured user bindings | `(let [p__1 10] (#(+ p__1 %) 2))` evaluated to `4` instead of `12`; `(let [p__1 10] (#(let [p__1 20] (+ p__1 %)) 2))` evaluated to `40` instead of `22` | Parse-local unforgeable `FnArgRef` + `collect-used-syms` + `fresh-param-sym` (`p<k>__<n>#`, `rest__<n>#`) + `resolve-fn-args` (`src/cljc/yang/clojure/reader.cljc:452-575`) | `b5-anon-fn-capture-avoiding-and-deterministic` GREEN on JVM & Node (incl. `12`, `22`, `33`, `66`, `305`, determinism, `#(#{% %1})` duplicate check) |\n37\t| **B-6** | `'` in `macro-terminating?` split `x'`; backtick `` ` `` threw unconditional error; `#^` missing; `@x` emitted `'deref` | `\"x'\"` threw `EOF while reading quote`; `\"foo'bar\"` read `foo`; `` \"`1\" `` threw unsupported error | Removed `39` (`'`) from `macro-terminating?`, added portable `syntax-quote*` preserving `numeric-carrier?` scalars/collections/metadata/auto-gensym, restored `#^`, `#<`, `@x` → `clojure.core/deref` (`src/cljc/yang/clojure/reader.cljc:111-129,578-705,805-845`) | `b6-lexical-compatibility-and-syntax-quote` (incl. 33-case differential parity vs `tools.reader`) GREEN on JVM & Node |\n38\t| **B-7** | Gate 5 test previously computed `(+ ... 0.5)` *after* resume | Evidence gap: pre-pause integral float never crossed pause/snapshot | Added `gate5-pre-pause-integral-float-across-continuation-and-snapshot` (`test/yang/clojure_float_kind_test.cljc:600-703`) covering direct pause/resume + UCF `lift-task`→`cbor/encode`→`cbor/decode`→`lower-task`→resume for `2.0`, `5.0`, `-0.0` | GREEN on JVM & Node (existing `gate5-parked-float-result-crosses-the-round` retained intact) |\n39\t\n40\t---\n41\t\n42\t## 3. TDD RED Evidence (Locked Before r2 Production Edits)\n43\t\n44\tAll RED logs are preserved under `collab/yang-clojure/1795710808000-floatkind-evidence/`:\n45\t\n46\t| Host | Command | Result | Log File |\n47\t|---|---|---|---|\n48\t| **JVM RED** | `clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-float-kind-test` | **27 tests, 445 assertions, 88 failures, 14 errors** (`RC=1`) | `collab/yang-clojure/1795710808000-floatkind-evidence/red-jvm-b2-b7.log` |\n49\t| **Node RED** | `clojure -Srepro -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test --config-merge '{:autorun false}' && node target/node-tests.